lifeos-nix patch f-cron-breaker-halfopen — Pulse cron circuit breaker gets a half-open probe

PROBLEM
  pulse.ts cron scheduler trips a circuit breaker after MAX_FAILURES (3) consecutive
  job failures and then SKIPS the job on every subsequent tick. The failure counter
  only resets on a successful run — but a skipped job never runs, so it can never reset
  itself. A transient failure spike (e.g. mid-migration) therefore deadlocks the job
  permanently: it stays skipped and /healthz stays "degraded" until someone manually
  resets state.json. Observed on the migrated box 2026-08-11: cost-aggregation,
  healthcheck, poller-meta-monitor all stuck since 2026-08-09 (3 failures each) even
  though all three run cleanly when invoked by hand. The healthcheck job itself was
  among the stuck ones, so the daemon could not even alert on its own degradation.

FIX (1 file)
  pulse.ts — when the breaker is open (consecutiveFailures >= MAX_FAILURES), skip only
  until BREAKER_COOLDOWN_MS (30 min) has elapsed since the last attempt, then fall
  through for ONE half-open probe run. Success resets the counter (existing path);
  another failure re-arms the cooldown (lastRun updates on the failed attempt). The
  breaker still prevents tight-loop retries of a genuinely broken job, but now
  self-heals once the underlying cause clears — no manual state.json reset needed.
  Complements the existing missing-script preflight (issue #1392), unchanged.

diff --git a/LifeOS/install/LIFEOS/PULSE/pulse.ts b/LifeOS/install/LIFEOS/PULSE/pulse.ts
--- a/LifeOS/install/LIFEOS/PULSE/pulse.ts
+++ b/LifeOS/install/LIFEOS/PULSE/pulse.ts
@@ -354,6 +354,12 @@
 const STATE_PATH = join(PULSE_DIR, "state", "state.json")
 const PID_PATH = join(PULSE_DIR, "state", "pulse.pid")
 const MAX_FAILURES = 3
+// Half-open circuit breaker: once a job trips MAX_FAILURES, do NOT skip it
+// forever — it could never run to reset its own counter, so a transient failure
+// spike would deadlock the job permanently (healthz degraded until manual reset).
+// After this cooldown since the last attempt, allow ONE probe run; success resets
+// the counter, another failure re-arms the cooldown.
+const BREAKER_COOLDOWN_MS = 30 * 60_000 // 30 min
 const MAX_SLEEP_MS = 60_000
 const MIN_SLEEP_MS = 1_000
 
@@ -902,10 +908,17 @@
       if (!isDue(job.schedule, now, jobState?.lastRun)) continue
 
       if ((jobState?.consecutiveFailures ?? 0) >= MAX_FAILURES) {
-        log("warn", `Skipping ${job.name}: ${jobState!.consecutiveFailures} consecutive failures`, {
-          lastResult: jobState!.lastResult,
+        // Half-open: skip until the cooldown elapses, then fall through for one probe run.
+        if (Date.now() - (jobState?.lastRun ?? 0) < BREAKER_COOLDOWN_MS) {
+          log("warn", `Skipping ${job.name}: ${jobState!.consecutiveFailures} consecutive failures (breaker cooldown)`, {
+            lastResult: jobState!.lastResult,
+            subsystem: "cron",
+          })
+          continue
+        }
+        log("info", `Half-open probe for ${job.name} after cooldown (${jobState!.consecutiveFailures} consecutive failures)`, {
+          subsystem: "cron",
         })
-        continue
       }
 
       log("info", `Running: ${job.name}`, { type: job.type, subsystem: "cron" })
